{title: Almost Persuaded}
{artist: Philip P. Bliss}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Five (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing Company, 1955), # 70)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Almost persuaded [Em]now [D]to be[G]lieve;
[G]Almost persuaded [D]Christ to re[G]ceive;
[C]Seems now some soul to [G]say,
[D]Go, Spirit, [G]go Thy way,
[G]Some [Am]more con[C]venient [G]day
[G]On Thee I’ll call.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Almost persuaded, [Em]come, [D]come to[G]day;
[G]Almost persuaded, [D]turn not a[G]way;
[C]Jesus invites you [G]here,
[D]Angels are [G]lingering near
[G]Prayers [Am]rise from [C]hearts so [G]dear;
[G]O wanderer, come!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Almost persuaded, [Em]har[D]vest is [G]past!
[G]Almost persuaded, [D]doom comes at [G]last!
[C]Almost cannot a[G]vail;
[D]Almost is [G]but to fail!
[G]Sad, [Am]sad, that [C]bitter [G]wail—
[G]Almost, but lost!
{end_of_verse}
